    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CLINICAL SUMMARY - Stokes-Maldonado Medical Group**\n\n**Patient:** Tammy Armstrong \n**DOB:** 11/07/1962 \n**Sex:** F \n**MRN:** 877792 \n\n---\n\n**Encounters:** \n\n- **2025-10-26** \n - **Reason for Visit:** Asthma \n - **Vitals:** BP 120/69, Wt 174 lbs \n - **Exam:** Lungs: Wheezes noted bilaterally, no rhonchi. Heart: Regular rate and rhythm. Abdomen: Soft, non-tender. Extremities: No edema. Skin: No rashes. \n\n- **2024-11-17** \n - **Reason for Visit:** Asthma \n - **Vitals:** BP 113/69, Wt 176 lbs \n - **Exam:** Lungs: Clear to auscultation, no wheezes. Heart: Normal S1, S2. Abdomen: Soft, non-tender. Extremities: No edema. Skin: Clear. \n\n- **2023-12-10** \n - **Reason for Visit:** Asthma \n - **Vitals:** BP 112/71, Wt 179 lbs \n - **Exam:** Lungs: Mild expiratory wheezing, no rhonchi. Heart: Regular rate and rhythm. Abdomen: Soft, non-tender. Extremities: No edema. Skin: No rashes. \n\n- **2023-01-01** \n - **Reason for Visit:** Asthma \n - **Vitals:** BP 122/80, Wt 177 lbs \n - **Exam:** Lungs: Mild expiratory wheezing, no rhonchi. Heart: Regular rate and rhythm. Abdomen: Soft, non-tender. Extremities: No edema. Skin: Clear. \n\n---\n\n**Assessment/Plan:** \n\n- **Asthma:** \n - Currently controlled, requiring 3 steroid bursts per year \n - Emergency room visit for asthma exacerbation 8.1 years ago \n - On biologic therapy \n - Medications: albuterol 90 mcg as needed for acute symptoms \n\n- **Social History:** \n - Tobacco use: Chewing tobacco, several times per day, started on June 1, 2018 \n - Alcohol consumption: Approximately 1 drink per week \n\n- **Family History:** \n - Mother has a history of myocardial infarction at the age of 80, currently living \n\n- **General Observations:** \n - Tammy reports occasional mild headaches and fatigue, likely related to stress. \n - Blood pressure has been stable, with readings within the normal range during all visits. \n - Weight has remained relatively stable, ranging from 174 to 179 lbs. \n\n---\n\n**Clinical Summary:** \n\nTammy Armstrong, a 62-year-old female, has been under my care for her asthma, which was diagnosed on May 11, 2020. She has maintained good control of her asthma with the use of albuterol 90 mcg as needed and biologic therapy. Over the past few years, she has required three steroid bursts annually. An emergency room visit for an asthma exacerbation occurred 8.1 years ago, but she has since remained stable.\n\nHer recent visits show that she has been managing her asthma well, with no acute exacerbations reported. Her physical examinations have consistently shown clear lung s"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "RECEIVED 4  ##\nounds with mild expiratory wheezing noted on some occasions. Vital signs have remained stable, and her weight has fluctuated slightly, but within a normal range.\n\nSocially, Tammy has been using chewing tobacco several times per day since June 1, 2018. She also reports consuming approximately one alcoholic drink per week. These habits have been documented, and appropriate counseling has been provided during her visits.\n\nFamily history is significant for myocardial infarction in her mother, who was diagnosed at the age of and remains alive. Tammy has occasional mild headaches and fatigue, which she attributes stress.\n\nIn summary, Tammy's asthma is well-controlled with current therapies. She has been compliant with her medications and has not required any emergency interventions recently. Continued monitoring and management of her asthma, along with ongoing efforts to address her tobacco use, are recommended.\n"
